# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# Retro Box
# Each install has its own config (the installer creates it from
# config.example.yaml). Keep personal configs out of the repo.
config.yaml
# The once-only copy of the config from before automation first edited it.
config.yaml.bak
# Generated filler clips (created by `retrobox --generate-assets`).
retrobox/assets/*.mp4
# ...but the boot splash is a source asset, not a generated one.
!retrobox/assets/boot_splash.mp4

# --- Unattended installer credentials ----------------------------------------
# THIS REPO IS PUBLIC.
#
# installer/autoinstall.yaml.template is committed and holds only placeholders.
# The rendered answer file holds a real password hash and a real SSH public key
# and must never be committed. This rule and that template belong to the same
# commit, so there is no window in which one exists without the other.
#
# Regenerate instead of recovering: installer/make-autoinstall.sh
installer/autoinstall.yaml
# Built boot media (multi-GB ISOs and stick images).
installer/build/

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
# Update progress, written next to the config so a reloaded page can
# pick a running update back up. Not something to commit.
.retrobox-update.json
# A network change on trial, written next to the config so the request that
# keeps it can find the one that started it. It holds the previous contents
# of the netplan files - which for wifi is the household's password - so it
# is 0600 on the box and it never goes near this repository.
.retrobox-network.json
